It's a Dine and Dash!

104
00:08:10,880 --> 00:08:12,220
Catch those criminals!

105
00:08:13,900 --> 00:08:17,360
Wow, ramen sure is good!
I know, right? Worth it!

106
00:08:18,360 --> 00:08:19,190
Criminals?

107
00:08:19,273 --> 00:08:20,103
They're just kids!

108
00:08:24,120 --> 00:08:26,977
Damn it, how did those little
pests sneak through the gate again?

109
00:08:27,060 --> 00:08:29,317
I've had enough of their
antics for a lifetime!

110
00:08:29,400 --> 00:08:30,757
Don't let them get away!

111
00:08:30,840 --> 00:08:32,237
I don't care if they're kids!

112
00:08:32,320 --> 00:08:33,980
They belong in a damn jail!

113
00:08:35,760 --> 00:08:38,560
Did they realize they
were on the fourth floor?

114
00:08:39,500 --> 00:08:41,540
Because that is a long fall!

115
00:08:41,880 --> 00:08:45,420
The window is a mess, but we
lost 26 bowls of ramen too!

116
00:08:46,540 --> 00:08:47,980
Sir, look at this.

117
00:08:48,140 --> 00:08:49,846
Those kids left a weird note.

118
00:08:53,820 --> 00:08:56,160
What is a treasure tab?

119
00:09:01,540 --> 00:09:02,370
Wait.

120
00:09:02,900 --> 00:09:03,730
Sabo?

121
00:09:03,940 --> 00:09:05,520
I can't believe it's him.

122
00:09:05,680 --> 00:09:08,460
Please come back. It's you. You're alive.

123
00:09:09,980 --> 00:09:11,380
Let's go home.

124
00:09:12,320 --> 00:09:13,440
The hell is this?

125
00:09:13,720 --> 00:09:15,537
Are you friends with that old dude, Sabo?

126
00:09:15,620 --> 00:09:16,855
I think he knows you.

127
00:09:17,340 --> 00:09:20,164
He's confusing me with
someone else, that's all.

128
00:09:22,160 --> 00:09:22,990
No!

129
00:09:23,160 --> 00:09:24,200
Sabo, come back!

130
00:09:35,820 --> 00:09:36,650
Sabo.

131
00:09:37,960 --> 00:09:40,400
We will have a visit this spring.

132
00:09:41,620 --> 00:09:42,920
Dogra! Mangra!

133
00:09:43,460 --> 00:09:45,680
What is Goa? A country?

134
00:09:45,920 --> 00:09:48,400
Uh, that's the country we live in.

135
00:09:48,620 --> 00:09:52,738
Mount Grove, Windmill Village, and
Great Terminal are all part of Goa.

136
00:09:52,900 --> 00:09:54,240
Hmph, I knew that.

137
00:09:54,500 --> 00:09:56,377
It must be the end of the world.

138
00:09:56,460 --> 00:10:00,077
I wasn't even sure you could read,
and now you're reading the paper.

139
00:10:00,160 --> 00:10:02,760
Frankly, it's kinda creeping me out. Oh.

140
00:10:04,060 --> 00:10:04,890
Anyway,

141
00:10:04,973 --> 00:10:06,877
they're making a big
deal about this visit,

142
00:10:06,960 --> 00:10:10,997
but it's not like they're gonna haul
their asses all the way to our mountain.

143
00:10:11,080 --> 00:10:14,315
Not that I'd want to see
those pompous bastards anyway.

144
00:10:15,060 --> 00:10:16,200
Celestial dragons?

145
00:10:16,540 --> 00:10:17,440
No thanks.

146
00:10:27,900 --> 00:10:28,917
You're wrong.

147
00:10:29,000 --> 00:10:30,500
I'm not hiding anything.

148
00:10:32,760 --> 00:10:33,920
That's cool, then.

149
00:10:34,740 --> 00:10:36,760
Come on, how stupid can you get?

150
00:10:36,960 --> 00:10:38,320
He's full of it.

151
00:10:38,720 --> 00:10:39,980
Damn it, Sabo.

152
00:10:40,120 --> 00:10:42,355
We can't keep secrets from each other.

153
00:10:43,780 --> 00:10:44,760
So talk!

154
00:10:48,860 --> 00:10:51,220
There's nothing for me to tell you.

155
00:10:51,480 --> 00:10:54,774
You trying to pick a fight
with me, spit it out already!

156
00:10:55,460 --> 00:10:58,220
Okay, okay, just stop killing me!

157
00:11:02,560 --> 00:11:04,220
The son of a noble?

158
00:11:06,180 --> 00:11:07,180
Who is?

159
00:11:07,540 --> 00:11:08,580
I am!

160
00:11:10,940 --> 00:11:11,770
Hmm, so?

161
00:11:12,100 --> 00:11:14,806
If you don't care, then
why didn't you ask me?

162
00:11:17,560 --> 00:11:20,400
The truth is, both my
parents are still alive.

163
00:11:20,920 --> 00:11:22,520
So yeah, I'm not an orphan.

164
00:11:23,100 --> 00:11:26,453
That means I lied about growing
up in Grey Terminal, too.

165
00:11:26,960 --> 00:11:29,254
And that guy who was calling out to me?

166
00:11:30,680 --> 00:11:31,720
That was my dad.

167
00:11:33,620 --> 00:11:34,450
I'm sorry.

168
00:11:34,720 --> 00:11:37,955
I know I've been lying to
you guys for a long time now.

169
00:11:38,240 --> 00:11:41,017
Well, he said he's sorry,
so we gotta forgive him.

170
00:11:41,100 --> 00:11:44,218
I'm not forgiving anyone
till I hear the whole story.

171
00:11:44,440 --> 00:11:46,616
If you're really from a noble family,

172
00:11:46,780 --> 00:11:49,839
why would you want to live
in some crappy junk heap?

173
00:11:51,680 --> 00:11:54,092
Because I ran away from home, that's why.

174
00:11:58,960 --> 00:12:01,400
You understand, don't you, Sabo?

175
00:12:03,120 --> 00:12:07,520
A noble must be a gentleman,
educated, well-mannered, and wise.

176
00:12:07,680 --> 00:12:12,000
And then, when you're older, you can
marry a girl from a royal family.

177
00:12:12,100 --> 00:12:14,477
That will make Mommy and Daddy very happy.

178
00:12:14,560 --> 00:12:17,266
Of course, I'm sure
you'll be very happy, too.

179
00:12:20,860 --> 00:12:21,860
Hello? Hello?

180
00:12:22,600 --> 00:12:23,430
The Lick?

181
00:12:24,440 --> 00:12:26,320
I cannot afford this.

182
00:12:26,520 --> 00:12:27,400
What a mess.

183
00:12:30,940 --> 00:12:31,770
Hey, Dad.

184
00:12:31,853 --> 00:12:32,780
Look at this.

185
00:12:32,900 --> 00:12:33,959
I drew it for you.

186
00:12:41,500 --> 00:12:44,040
Your father is having
a trying day at work.

187
00:12:44,240 --> 00:12:47,920
Sabo, if you have time to draw
this, you have time to study.

188
00:12:59,280 --> 00:13:00,240
Hey, you!

189
00:13:01,800 --> 00:13:06,200
I'm from the royal family, and that
means you have to do everything I say.

190
00:13:06,760 --> 00:13:08,289
Carry me back to my house.

191
00:13:14,680 --> 00:13:15,860
How dare you!

192
00:13:16,200 --> 00:13:20,340
I'm related to the king, and I want
a piggyback ride right now! Stop!

193
00:13:20,660 --> 00:13:21,660
Get off of me!

194
00:13:28,680 --> 00:13:31,200
You nobles think you're so hot, don't you?

195
00:13:32,060 --> 00:13:33,472
This ought to teach you!

196
00:13:42,920 --> 00:13:44,820
My son has royal blood!

197
00:13:44,980 --> 00:13:48,077
I won't stand for you spilling
it on the pavement, you old!

198
00:13:48,160 --> 00:13:52,277
Sabo, tell me you didn't get in a fight
with this boy from the royal family!

199
00:13:52,360 --> 00:13:53,980
Well, kind of.

200
00:13:54,420 --> 00:13:57,780
I mean, he attacked me with
this scary knife, so...

201
00:14:03,440 --> 00:14:05,820
My son can be such a little beast.

202
00:14:06,020 --> 00:14:07,040
I blame myself.

203
00:14:07,240 --> 00:14:08,697
I do hope you aren't hurt.

204
00:14:08,780 --> 00:14:10,180
It's terrible, I know.

205
00:14:10,340 --> 00:14:11,337
Please forgive us.

206
00:14:11,420 --> 00:14:13,857
I assure you he will be
punished severely for this.

207
00:14:13,940 --> 00:14:16,137
I'll do anything I can
to make things right.

208
00:14:16,220 --> 00:14:19,867
Shall we go to the doctor to
make sure your son isn't injured?

209
00:14:20,660 --> 00:14:23,640
Then I realized they love their money,

210
00:14:24,420 --> 00:14:27,040
their property, their status?

211
00:14:28,540 --> 00:14:30,120
but not their son.

212
00:14:33,600 --> 00:14:37,257
If I couldn't marry into a royal
family, I was useless to them.

213
00:14:37,340 --> 00:14:40,977
They tried to teach me culture
and literature and all that stuff.

214
00:14:41,060 --> 00:14:43,317
But I guess I didn't
learn fast enough because

215
00:14:43,400 --> 00:14:45,812
they were always arguing and getting mad.

216
00:14:45,900 --> 00:14:48,547
That family had no place
for someone like me.

217
00:14:49,260 --> 00:14:53,920
I know you guys have it worse, but even
if I had parents, I was still alone.

218
00:14:55,260 --> 00:15:00,200
I heard that you've been sneaking out
behind my back, going goodness knows where.

219
00:15:00,920 --> 00:15:02,257
I shouldn't have to tell you this,

220
00:15:02,340 --> 00:15:06,105
but stay away from Great Terminal
if you know it's good for you.

221
00:15:06,860 --> 00:15:10,217
We nobles are privileged to live in
Hightown with the king and his family.

222
00:15:10,300 --> 00:15:13,337
It's a life the people down
there can only dream of.

223
00:15:13,420 --> 00:15:17,140
By the same token, you do
not belong in their world.

224
00:15:19,360 --> 00:15:23,417
Well, at least the people in Great
Terminal know what it means to be free.

225
00:15:23,500 --> 00:15:25,517
If the nobles in Hightown
didn't spend their

226
00:15:25,600 --> 00:15:27,757
whole lives licking the
boots of the royal family,

227
00:15:27,840 --> 00:15:31,369
Maybe they'd look up and see
that there's more to the world.

228
00:15:32,140 --> 00:15:33,540
Man, I had no idea.

229
00:15:34,580 --> 00:15:36,280
Ace, Luffy, listen.

230
00:15:37,140 --> 00:15:39,980
The three of us, we're
gonna leave this country.

231
00:15:40,680 --> 00:15:43,460
We're gonna sail the
seas and see the world.

232
00:15:43,720 --> 00:15:47,780
And once I've done it all, I'm
gonna write a book for kids like me.

233
00:15:48,460 --> 00:15:50,877
Cause studying is fun when
you're learning about adventure,

234
00:15:50,960 --> 00:15:52,357
and we're gonna have lots of them.

235
00:15:52,440 --> 00:15:53,960
We're gonna be pirates!

236
00:16:00,580 --> 00:16:01,992
You don't gotta tell me.

237
00:16:02,160 --> 00:16:03,817
I'm gonna be a pirate anyway.

238
00:16:03,900 --> 00:16:07,937
I'll be so tough that all the other pirates
and all the marines will bow at my feet.

239
00:16:08,020 --> 00:16:10,373
Everyone in the world will know my name.

240
00:16:10,560 --> 00:16:13,678
That's gonna be the legacy
I leave behind when I die.

241
00:16:13,820 --> 00:16:15,597
I don't care if people hate me.

242
00:16:15,680 --> 00:16:17,877
I don't care if they
wish I'd never been born.

243
00:16:17,960 --> 00:16:19,431
But they won't ignore me.

244
00:16:20,600 --> 00:16:23,894
That's what it means to be
strong, to be a great pirate.

245
00:16:24,000 --> 00:16:26,457
I won't ever lose and
I won't ever run away.

246
00:16:26,540 --> 00:16:31,840
Who cares if the world fears me or respects
me or whatever I'm gonna be a legend?

247
00:16:34,080 --> 00:16:36,260
Then I know what I'm gonna be Tim!

248
00:16:49,880 --> 00:16:53,400
You dork just gotta try
and show me up, don't you?

249
00:16:56,040 --> 00:16:57,897
I don't know if you'll be a king or not.

250
00:16:57,980 --> 00:16:59,677
But you're gonna do something crazy!

251
00:16:59,760 --> 00:17:01,289
I know that much for sure.

252
00:17:02,560 --> 00:17:05,237
We all want to be pirates
together though, don't we?

253
00:17:05,320 --> 00:17:09,908
We're only saving for one ship But what
if all three of us want to be captain?

254
00:17:10,080 --> 00:17:11,737
Damn it, I never thought of that.

255
00:17:11,820 --> 00:17:15,237
Sabo, I always figured you'd
be the navigator on my ship!

256
00:17:15,320 --> 00:17:17,777
You guys are welcome to join my crew?

257
00:17:17,860 --> 00:17:18,980
No thanks!

258
00:17:21,580 --> 00:17:24,286
Well, we'll figure it
out when the time comes.

259
00:17:24,440 --> 00:17:28,028
Maybe we'll leave on one ship
and maybe we'll leave on three.

260
00:17:29,180 --> 00:17:31,720
Oh, you stole that from Dadan, huh?

261
00:17:32,300 --> 00:17:34,100
Let me tell you guys a secret.

262
00:17:36,560 --> 00:17:39,760
All it takes to become
brothers is to share some sake.

263
00:17:40,440 --> 00:17:41,270
Whoa, really?

264
00:17:41,600 --> 00:17:42,760
That's so cool!

265
00:17:43,020 --> 00:17:46,777
We may sail in different seas with
different crews on different ships.

266
00:17:46,860 --> 00:17:50,657
But wherever we go and
whatever adventures we have.

267
00:17:50,740 --> 00:17:54,280
We'll always be brothers and
nobody can take that away.

268
00:17:56,760 --> 00:18:00,057
From now on, we're
honest-to-goodness brothers.

269
00:18:00,140 --> 00:18:01,800
Cheers to that!

270
00:18:08,620 --> 00:18:09,450
Brothers!

271
00:18:18,000 --> 00:18:20,040
Thank you.

272
00:18:48,640 --> 00:18:51,440
Thank you.

273
00:19:30,140 --> 00:19:31,540
¶¶

274
00:19:54,060 --> 00:19:55,357
Give him back, you jerk!

275
00:19:55,440 --> 00:19:57,917
What do you mean, give
him back, you filthy rat?

276
00:19:58,000 --> 00:19:59,320
Sabo is my son,

277
00:19:59,480 --> 00:20:03,817
which means that he's obligated to live
on the path that I have prepared for him.

278
00:20:03,900 --> 00:20:07,757
You should be ashamed, steering him
toward the life of a petty thief.

279
00:20:07,840 --> 00:20:10,075
You're both nothing but wannabe thugs.

280
00:20:10,420 --> 00:20:12,460
Why did you do it? For my money?

281
00:20:12,640 --> 00:20:14,080
Screw your damn money!

282
00:20:16,640 --> 00:20:20,540
You foolish pirate, quit knocking
that kid around so carelessly.

283
00:20:20,860 --> 00:20:24,684
You'll get that delinquent's
disgusting blood on my nice clothes.

284
00:20:24,840 --> 00:20:25,740
Hey, Ace!

285
00:20:26,480 --> 00:20:27,940
Hey, come back here!

286
00:20:28,640 --> 00:20:29,740
Stop this, okay?

287
00:20:29,980 --> 00:20:31,921
Nobody tempted me to do anything.

288
00:20:32,180 --> 00:20:34,400
I only ran away because I wanted to.

289
00:20:34,600 --> 00:20:36,397
I'll be dealing with you later, Sabo.

290
00:20:36,480 --> 00:20:37,310
Take him!

291
00:20:38,520 --> 00:20:40,957
Deal with the other two
however you see fit.

292
00:20:41,040 --> 00:20:42,580
Not a problem, sir.

293
00:20:42,880 --> 00:20:44,957
You've already paid us quite handsomely.

294
00:20:45,040 --> 00:20:48,216
We'll make sure these two
never bother your boy again.

295
00:20:48,320 --> 00:20:50,260
I'll spare you the gory details.

296
00:20:52,080 --> 00:20:53,140
Wait, Blue Jam!

297
00:20:53,360 --> 00:20:54,337
Please don't hurt them!

298
00:20:54,420 --> 00:20:55,297
Call them off, Dad!

299
00:20:55,380 --> 00:20:57,660
I get it! Please stop! Huh?

300
00:20:57,860 --> 00:20:59,680
What do you mean, you get it?

301
00:21:01,520 --> 00:21:03,060
Don't you dare, Sabo!

302
00:21:04,320 --> 00:21:06,600
I'll do whatever you want me to, okay?

303
00:21:07,480 --> 00:21:09,597
I'll live whatever life you've mapped out.

304
00:21:09,680 --> 00:21:13,820
Just please, I'm begging
you, don't hurt my friends?

305
00:21:14,840 --> 00:21:16,217
They've done nothing wrong!

306
00:21:16,300 --> 00:21:18,157
I can't stand this!

307
00:21:18,240 --> 00:21:20,020
Those two are my brothers!

308
00:21:21,060 --> 00:21:22,000
Sabo, no!

309
00:21:23,240 --> 00:21:24,070
Oh?

310
00:21:24,153 --> 00:21:26,337
If that's what you want, then go home!

311
00:21:26,420 --> 00:21:30,680
And promise you'll stop playing
pirate with Lolice in this trash heap?

312
00:21:32,780 --> 00:21:33,610
No!

313
00:21:33,780 --> 00:21:35,380
Don't do it! Shut up, kid!

314
00:21:36,000 --> 00:21:37,060
Damn it, Sabo!

315
00:21:37,280 --> 00:21:38,110
Run away from them!

316
00:21:38,193 --> 00:21:40,474
Luffy and I can take care of ourselves.

317
00:21:40,700 --> 00:21:41,759
This is your life.

318
00:21:41,860 --> 00:21:43,036
You have to be free!

319
00:21:43,320 --> 00:21:45,420
He's right! Don't go!

320
00:21:46,140 --> 00:21:49,820
Are you going to abandon all
your dreams just like that? Sabo!

321
00:21:54,000 --> 00:21:54,830
Sabo!

322
00:22:00,160 --> 00:22:00,990
Sabo!

323
00:22:08,180 --> 00:22:11,397
Hey, Captain, what do you want
us to do with the other ones?

324
00:22:11,480 --> 00:22:14,240
We'll take them back to
the hideout. Yes, sir.

325
00:22:16,160 --> 00:22:17,440
Bastard, untie me!

326
00:22:17,740 --> 00:22:18,916
Come here and fight!

327
00:22:19,060 --> 00:22:20,766
I'm not gonna lose this time!

328
00:22:21,000 --> 00:22:23,480
It must be awful nice to be a noble.

329
00:22:23,960 --> 00:22:25,431
Wouldn't you punks agree?

330
00:22:26,040 --> 00:22:29,277
To them, we're no different than
the piles of garbage we live in.

331
00:22:29,360 --> 00:22:32,117
They just sit back while
we do all the dirty work.

332
00:22:32,200 --> 00:22:35,237
It's a pretty cushy life
your buddy's living, I'd say.

333
00:22:35,320 --> 00:22:37,357
You got no clue what you're talking about!

334
00:22:37,440 --> 00:22:40,357
Pirate life is way better
than being a stupid noble!

335
00:22:40,440 --> 00:22:41,675
Sabo said so himself!

336
00:22:41,900 --> 00:22:45,097
You kids are so hopeless I
can't help feeling bad for you.

337
00:22:45,180 --> 00:22:46,917
Hey, untie their robes in quick.

338
00:22:47,000 --> 00:22:47,830
Yes, sir.

339
00:22:47,913 --> 00:22:51,737
Why do you think a kid from a noble family
ran off to a place like Grey Terminal?

340
00:22:51,820 --> 00:22:54,757
Did you think he just wanted
to make some new friends?

341
00:22:54,840 --> 00:22:57,657
He was mocking you and
all the other people here,

342
00:22:57,740 --> 00:23:00,858
just like adult nobles do
when they're feeling bored.

343
00:23:01,380 --> 00:23:03,145
Real sorry to break it to you.

344
00:23:03,300 --> 00:23:04,737
That boy's no friend of yours.

345
00:23:04,820 --> 00:23:05,650
You're lying.

346
00:23:05,900 --> 00:23:07,797
Sabo would never pull a stunt like that.

347
00:23:07,880 --> 00:23:08,710
He's right.

348
00:23:08,793 --> 00:23:09,877
He said we were brothers.

349
00:23:09,960 --> 00:23:10,790
You heard him.

350
00:23:10,873 --> 00:23:11,800
Yeah, guess so.

351
00:23:12,020 --> 00:23:13,314
Whatever you kids say.

352
00:23:13,940 --> 00:23:18,797
But in any case, you boys aren't going to
bother him or his family anymore, are you?

353
00:23:18,880 --> 00:23:20,357
Because if that's the plan,

354
00:23:20,440 --> 00:23:23,537
I'm afraid I'd have to take you
both out right here and now.

355
00:23:23,620 --> 00:23:25,597
If you really think of
him as your brother,

356
00:23:25,680 --> 00:23:28,327
it'd be best for everyone
to leave him alone.

357
00:23:29,300 --> 00:23:30,237
Leave him alone?

358
00:23:30,320 --> 00:23:31,555
What about our dream?

359
00:23:32,060 --> 00:23:32,890
No!

360
00:23:32,973 --> 00:23:34,457
Sabo told us that he hates Hightown!

361
00:23:34,540 --> 00:23:36,977
Look, if you really care
about this Sabo kid,

362
00:23:37,060 --> 00:23:39,477
then you gotta let him
go live his own life.

363
00:23:39,560 --> 00:23:41,437
You'll understand when you grow up.

364
00:23:41,520 --> 00:23:42,350
Anyway,

365
00:23:42,433 --> 00:23:44,897
until recently I had a
bone to pick with you

366
00:23:44,980 --> 00:23:47,237
after what happened with
Portjami and our money.

367
00:23:47,320 --> 00:23:48,849
But I'm over all that now.

368
00:23:49,100 --> 00:23:52,157
In fact, I'm kind of impressed at
how tough you little punks are.

369
00:23:52,240 --> 00:23:54,537
Which is why I wanted
to ask you something.

370
00:23:54,620 --> 00:23:56,620
It might just be worth your while.

371
00:23:56,780 --> 00:23:59,251
Thanks to you boys, I'm kinda shorthanded.

372
00:23:59,560 --> 00:24:02,617
So, how would you feel
about doing a job for me?

373
00:24:02,700 --> 00:24:03,720
Don't worry.

374
00:24:04,140 --> 00:24:05,477
It's a short, easy gig.

375
00:24:05,560 --> 00:24:08,442
There's actually not really
much danger involved.

376
00:24:08,880 --> 00:24:10,997
On that barrel's a map of Gray Terminal.

377
00:24:11,080 --> 00:24:15,277
You just have to carry packages to the
locations marked on the map with an X.

378
00:24:15,360 --> 00:24:16,242
You interested?

379
00:24:16,860 --> 00:24:17,840
Okay, sure.

380
00:24:18,980 --> 00:24:20,140
What about pay?

381
00:24:25,000 --> 00:24:26,640
My head is tired.

382
00:24:27,280 --> 00:24:29,377
Pulling stuff's no fun
if Sabo's not around.

383
00:24:29,460 --> 00:24:30,517
Just deal with it.

384
00:24:30,600 --> 00:24:31,617
I don't like this either.

385
00:24:31,700 --> 00:24:35,641
I'd much rather find Sabo and rescue
him, but Blue Jam had a point.

386
00:24:35,840 --> 00:24:38,075
We've got to let him live his own life

387
00:24:39,280 --> 00:24:40,680
Look give it some time.

388
00:24:40,840 --> 00:24:43,697
He's gonna be all right,
and if he doesn't like it,

389
00:24:43,780 --> 00:24:45,898
he can always come and join us again

390
00:24:46,240 --> 00:24:47,440
Until that happens.

391
00:24:47,740 --> 00:24:50,269
Let's keep putting
money in the pirate fund

392
00:24:51,960 --> 00:24:53,237
Believe what you want.

393
00:24:53,320 --> 00:24:55,037
It's still not Ace and Luffy's fault.

394
00:24:55,120 --> 00:24:56,217
Quit wasting our time.

395
00:24:56,300 --> 00:24:59,220
Tell us the truth Wait just a minute.

396
00:24:59,420 --> 00:25:01,297
Those scoundrels must have threatened you.

397
00:25:01,380 --> 00:25:03,357
They really have you wrapped
around their fingers.

398
00:25:03,440 --> 00:25:05,897
No, they aren't those
kind of people, okay?

399
00:25:05,980 --> 00:25:08,237
Any noble with a criminal
record to his name

400
00:25:08,320 --> 00:25:10,837
will damage his family's
hard-earned reputation.

401
00:25:10,920 --> 00:25:13,217
You would also be barred
from entering Hightown.

402
00:25:13,300 --> 00:25:15,037
Those two forced you to leave home?

403
00:25:15,120 --> 00:25:17,537
and get involved with their
atrocious acts of violence!

404
00:25:17,620 --> 00:25:19,326
against your better judgment.

405
00:25:19,420 --> 00:25:20,820
Isn't that right, Sabo?

406
00:25:22,420 --> 00:25:23,250
Hmm.

407
00:25:23,660 --> 00:25:24,600
Look here, son.

408
00:25:24,960 --> 00:25:28,537
The fate of your friends in Great
Terminal is in the hand of pirates.

409
00:25:28,620 --> 00:25:30,149
Those pirates work for me.

410
00:25:30,580 --> 00:25:32,639
All I need to do is give the order.

411
00:25:32,800 --> 00:25:35,212
If these slumberettes are that important,

412
00:25:35,380 --> 00:25:38,086
think long and hard about
what you have to do.

413
00:25:40,820 --> 00:25:43,460
You're a smart boy,
born to a great family.

414
00:25:43,720 --> 00:25:45,485
You already know what's right.

415
00:25:46,060 --> 00:25:47,957
You promised me you wouldn't hurt them.

416
00:25:48,040 --> 00:25:49,717
That's the only reason I came back here.

417
00:25:49,800 --> 00:25:52,297
You haven't changed at
all since I ran away.

418
00:25:52,380 --> 00:25:53,680
No one tempted me.

419
00:25:53,900 --> 00:25:56,460
I made every decision by my own free will.

420
00:25:59,300 --> 00:26:01,160
You disappoint me.

421
00:26:01,820 --> 00:26:03,540
I apologize, sir.

422
00:26:03,740 --> 00:26:06,397
I'm so ashamed that I
have such a foolish son.

423
00:26:06,480 --> 00:26:08,421
Surely you understand my dilemma.

424
00:26:09,100 --> 00:26:09,957
Of course.

425
00:26:10,040 --> 00:26:12,020
It must tear you apart inside.

426
00:26:13,280 --> 00:26:14,400
Don't you worry.

427
00:26:14,680 --> 00:26:16,798
I'll take care of all the paperwork.

428
00:26:18,960 --> 00:26:20,300
Welcome back, sir.

429
00:26:21,840 --> 00:26:23,020
Home at last.

430
00:26:23,220 --> 00:26:24,220
Let's go, Sabo.

431
00:26:24,360 --> 00:26:26,117
You've been gone quite some time.

432
00:26:26,200 --> 00:26:30,040
Ah, on second thought, don't
come in yet, you must be filthy.

433
00:26:30,700 --> 00:26:34,582
Hose yourself off in the yard
first, then come in and take a bath.

434
00:26:34,680 --> 00:26:37,974
We're all glad that you're
back home safe, young master.

435
00:26:38,540 --> 00:26:39,580
Oh, goodness!

436
00:26:39,880 --> 00:26:40,880
Is it really you?

437
00:26:40,980 --> 00:26:42,340
You've grown so big!

438
00:26:43,860 --> 00:26:44,760
Hello, Mom.

439
00:26:45,160 --> 00:26:47,920
Now, Stella, say hello
to your brother, Sabo.

440
00:26:48,060 --> 00:26:49,860
Nice to meet you, big brother.

441
00:26:50,240 --> 00:26:51,900
I'm Stella and I'm eight.

442
00:26:52,040 --> 00:26:52,922
What about you?

443
00:26:53,380 --> 00:26:54,380
What the hell?

444
00:26:56,200 --> 00:26:57,260
We adopted him.

445
00:26:57,420 --> 00:27:00,117
He's a promising boy from
another noble family.

446
00:27:00,200 --> 00:27:04,494
For reasons beyond understanding, his
parents suddenly became neglectful.

447
00:27:04,580 --> 00:27:07,080
So far, he's fit in extremely well.

448
00:27:07,460 --> 00:27:09,617
I imagine that if things
don't work out with

449
00:27:09,700 --> 00:27:11,597
you when it's time to choose a successor,

450
00:27:11,680 --> 00:27:12,777
then he would...

451
00:27:12,860 --> 00:27:14,760
No, no, never mind.

452
00:27:15,040 --> 00:27:16,158
I've said too much.

453
00:27:16,260 --> 00:27:18,037
Go and get settled in your room.

454
00:27:18,120 --> 00:27:20,708
You'll resume your
studies tomorrow morning.

455
00:27:29,620 --> 00:27:32,914
Are you going to abandon all
your dreams just like that?

456
00:27:35,560 --> 00:27:37,560
Hey, do you know what I heard?

457
00:27:37,740 --> 00:27:39,093
You're dumb as a brick.

458
00:27:40,640 --> 00:27:44,169
That's what Mama and Papa think,
in case you couldn't guess.

459
00:27:44,720 --> 00:27:46,740
But still, you sure are lucky.

460
00:27:47,080 --> 00:27:50,080
Tomorrow night, they're
taking care of the garbage.

461
00:27:50,340 --> 00:27:53,516
To think had you stayed in
Gray Terminal a day longer?

462
00:27:54,860 --> 00:27:57,331
You'd be dead like the rest of the crooks!

463
00:27:58,360 --> 00:27:59,190
Too bad!

464
00:27:59,273 --> 00:28:02,037
My life would be a lot easier
if you never came back.

465
00:28:02,120 --> 00:28:04,414
But I'm clever enough, so I'll make do.

466
00:28:05,280 --> 00:28:06,600
Hey, Al, stop!

467
00:28:07,060 --> 00:28:10,000
Let go of me or I'll tell
Papa What did you say?

468
00:28:10,200 --> 00:28:11,180
What's going on?

469
00:28:11,400 --> 00:28:14,560
You tell me everything
or I'll beat you up Wait!

470
00:28:14,920 --> 00:28:17,096
Tomorrow, there's going to be a fire!

471
00:28:17,520 --> 00:28:18,977
They're burning gray terminal.

472
00:28:19,060 --> 00:28:20,120
A fire?

473
00:28:20,260 --> 00:28:24,597
That's right You didn't hear about it
because you've been away for so long.

474
00:28:24,680 --> 00:28:27,327
The nobles in Hightown
decided it months ago.

475
00:28:27,520 --> 00:28:32,461
The world government is sending a group of
people to check out all of the East Blue.

476
00:28:32,880 --> 00:28:36,939
They're finally going to arrive and
go a kingdom three days from now.

477
00:28:37,100 --> 00:28:42,160
Rumor has it they have a world
noble, a celestial dragon with them.

478
00:28:42,460 --> 00:28:43,720
People are panicking.

479
00:28:43,980 --> 00:28:45,897
The members of the royal family don't want

480
00:28:45,980 --> 00:28:48,077
him to see all the dirty
parts of this country.

481
00:28:48,160 --> 00:28:51,840
So they made the obvious decision
to burn down Great Terminal.

482
00:28:52,340 --> 00:28:55,997
It's a surefire way to cleanse
this country of all its rubbish.

483
00:28:56,080 --> 00:28:59,037
There's no way they'd just burn
everything down without warning!

484
00:28:59,120 --> 00:29:00,957
Don't joke about something like that!

485
00:29:01,040 --> 00:29:03,617
There's a lot of people
living in Great Terminal.

486
00:29:03,700 --> 00:29:06,737
They can't just torch down their
homes because they feel like it!

487
00:29:06,820 --> 00:29:07,860
Get off of me!

488
00:29:08,140 --> 00:29:09,640
You really are stupid.

489
00:29:09,860 --> 00:29:12,389
Haven't you heard a
single thing I've said?

490
00:29:12,820 --> 00:29:14,640
All the shame of this country.

491
00:29:15,000 --> 00:29:16,977
Tomorrow they're gonna burn it all away.

492
00:29:17,060 --> 00:29:19,680
The people, too?

493
00:29:26,500 --> 00:29:27,960
Hey, wait up!

494
00:29:29,940 --> 00:29:31,220
Where are you going?

495
00:29:35,520 --> 00:29:37,873
You can't jump out the window like that!

496
00:29:42,280 --> 00:29:44,180
Wow, he's a goner.

497
00:29:44,400 --> 00:29:45,360
It's a lie.

498
00:29:45,560 --> 00:29:46,390
It's gotta be.

499
00:29:46,473 --> 00:29:48,655
They can't burn down a place that big.

500
00:29:48,800 --> 00:29:50,506
And someone would have heard.

501
00:29:55,840 --> 00:29:57,546
Soldiers from this afternoon.

502
00:29:58,600 --> 00:30:00,776
Are we sure we're ready for tomorrow?

503
00:30:00,880 --> 00:30:02,737
There can't be any miscalculations.

504
00:30:02,820 --> 00:30:06,137
We're ready on our end, but we're
stuck relying on the pirates.

505
00:30:06,220 --> 00:30:09,514
They have to burn the trash
precisely at the right time.

506
00:30:10,040 --> 00:30:10,870
Don't worry.

507
00:30:11,320 --> 00:30:13,137
Blue Jim and his men
have been placing boxes

508
00:30:13,220 --> 00:30:15,617
of oil and explosives
all over Gray Terminal.

509
00:30:15,700 --> 00:30:16,860
Just like we asked

510
00:30:18,680 --> 00:30:23,840
Blue Jam has a hand in this it must
be true, but why what's in it for him?

511
00:30:36,000 --> 00:30:39,520
Hey Ace, what do you think
Saba's doing? Seriously?

512
00:30:40,000 --> 00:30:40,830
Shut up.

513
00:30:40,913 --> 00:30:44,311
I Thought we had agreed to stop
worrying about him for now.

514
00:30:44,920 --> 00:30:45,750
Okay.

515
00:30:46,120 --> 00:30:49,720
Who knows, this could actually
work out better for him?

516
00:30:52,920 --> 00:30:53,940
Okay, think,

517
00:30:54,400 --> 00:30:56,637
if there was really going
to be a fire tonight,

518
00:30:56,720 --> 00:30:59,896
the people in the town would
be upset about it, right?

519
00:31:03,400 --> 00:31:04,697
Why, good morning?

520
00:31:04,780 --> 00:31:06,437
A good morning to you, sir!

521
00:31:06,520 --> 00:31:08,337
What a beautiful sunny day!

522
00:31:08,420 --> 00:31:09,317
Yes, lovely.

523
00:31:09,400 --> 00:31:13,357
What a relief, guess there's nothing
fishy happening today after all!

524
00:31:13,440 --> 00:31:15,320
I'll walk around for a bit.

525
00:31:18,340 --> 00:31:19,700
Today is windy.

526
00:31:20,680 --> 00:31:23,257
That's true, your majesty,
very windy indeed!

527
00:31:23,340 --> 00:31:26,417
Accidents can happen
easily on a day like this.

528
00:31:26,500 --> 00:31:28,837
Especially wildfires.

529
00:31:28,920 --> 00:31:31,157
How right you are, majesty!

530
00:31:31,240 --> 00:31:33,600
It's quite possible. What?

531
00:31:33,940 --> 00:31:35,587
Sabo snuck out of the house?

532
00:31:35,920 --> 00:31:37,737
He's such an ungrateful brat!

533
00:31:37,820 --> 00:31:40,417
All he cares about is playing
pirate with his friends!

534
00:31:40,500 --> 00:31:42,735
When he should stay at home and study.

535
00:31:42,920 --> 00:31:45,117
Have the police search the entire town.

536
00:31:45,200 --> 00:31:47,788
He couldn't have gotten
very far by himself.

537
00:31:49,140 --> 00:31:50,680
Um, excuse me.

538
00:31:50,860 --> 00:31:52,160
What do you want, kid?

539
00:31:52,480 --> 00:31:56,237
Did you know that there's supposed to
be a fire in Grey Terminal tonight?

540
00:31:56,320 --> 00:31:58,202
Of course I know about the fire.

541
00:31:58,520 --> 00:31:59,350
Why, what's wrong?

542
00:31:59,433 --> 00:32:00,398
Did they cancel it?

543
00:32:00,700 --> 00:32:01,700
He knows.

544
00:32:02,120 --> 00:32:04,473
Tell me, boy, whose family are you from?

545
00:32:05,400 --> 00:32:06,940
So, it's true.

546
00:32:09,000 --> 00:32:09,840
Hold on!

547
00:32:09,980 --> 00:32:11,217
Everyone knows, don't they?

548
00:32:11,300 --> 00:32:12,900
They have from the start.

549
00:32:13,300 --> 00:32:15,100
Look at them. They're smiling.

550
00:32:15,480 --> 00:32:18,117
They don't give a damn about
the people in Great Terminal.

551
00:32:18,200 --> 00:32:20,847
They're happy to see
them burn to the ground.

552
00:32:24,120 --> 00:32:27,080
You know, we've been waiting on you.

553
00:32:27,340 --> 00:32:29,677
Are there any more boxes
you need us to move?

554
00:32:29,760 --> 00:32:32,642
Yeah, and I've got a bigger
job for you later on.

555
00:32:32,760 --> 00:32:34,737
But we'll talk more about that tonight.

556
00:32:34,820 --> 00:32:36,840
Yes, I heard all about the fire.

557
00:32:37,040 --> 00:32:38,960
And you're not worried at all?

558
00:32:39,580 --> 00:32:41,874
Nobody in this town cares what happens?

559
00:32:41,960 --> 00:32:44,901
Nobody in town even thinks
of stopping this thing?

560
00:32:46,220 --> 00:32:47,860
That's admirable of you.

561
00:32:48,140 --> 00:32:50,022
You must have a very kind heart.

562
00:32:50,580 --> 00:32:53,300
But boy, please don't you say a word.

563
00:32:53,580 --> 00:32:56,404
It's important that we
all keep our mouths shut.

564
00:32:56,820 --> 00:33:01,526
Think what would happen if someone outside
of Hightown found out about the plan.

565
00:33:01,640 --> 00:33:03,420
You and I are special.

566
00:33:03,800 --> 00:33:05,800
We come from great noble families.

567
00:33:06,940 --> 00:33:07,980
Calm down.

568
00:33:09,420 --> 00:33:13,117
Ace Luffy there's something
wrong with this town something

569
00:33:13,200 --> 00:33:16,520
wrong with these people They
know people are gonna die.

570
00:33:16,640 --> 00:33:18,697
They're happy people are going to die.

571
00:33:18,780 --> 00:33:19,610
They're sick.

572
00:33:19,700 --> 00:33:22,960
This whole place is sick I
can't stay here any longer.

573
00:33:23,140 --> 00:33:24,846
I have to tell them right now

574
00:33:27,960 --> 00:33:31,800
Today of all days, why is
it so windy? That's him.

575
00:33:32,100 --> 00:33:33,177
That's the missing boy.

576
00:33:33,260 --> 00:33:34,400
Excuse me kid.

577
00:33:34,600 --> 00:33:36,012
You need to come with us

578
00:33:36,660 --> 00:33:38,200
Hey you stop running

579
00:33:38,960 --> 00:33:41,197
The nobles here don't
care who they killed.

580
00:33:41,280 --> 00:33:44,517
They'll burn a whole town alive
just because they don't like it.

581
00:33:44,600 --> 00:33:48,397
You've got to get out of Grey Terminal
and you've got to get out now.

582
00:33:48,480 --> 00:33:49,920
Hold on, Ace!

583
00:33:51,020 --> 00:33:52,360
Luffy, I'm coming!

584
00:33:54,120 --> 00:33:56,017
Why the hell would you want to do that?

585
00:33:56,100 --> 00:33:56,930
Not so loud.

586
00:33:57,360 --> 00:33:59,177
We've got to keep quiet about this.

587
00:33:59,260 --> 00:34:01,319
If anyone finds out, it won't work.

588
00:34:01,420 --> 00:34:02,817
You really are a Moon.

589
00:34:02,900 --> 00:34:04,377
I knew we shouldn't have trusted you.

590
00:34:04,460 --> 00:34:06,337
We've got to hurry and
tell everyone we can, Ace!

591
00:34:06,420 --> 00:34:07,557
I told you to keep quiet.

592
00:34:07,640 --> 00:34:08,660
Hey!

593
00:34:08,900 --> 00:34:09,760
Shut him up!

594
00:34:11,040 --> 00:34:13,334
I'm just following orders, same as you.

595
00:34:14,980 --> 00:34:16,451
In case you didn't guess,

596
00:34:16,740 --> 00:34:20,858
all those boxes you've been lugging
around are filled with explosives.

597
00:34:20,960 --> 00:34:21,940
You get it?

598
00:34:22,840 --> 00:34:25,860
Nothing will survive
that fire, and no one.

599
00:34:26,560 --> 00:34:28,900
But, Blue Jam, don't do it!

600
00:34:29,980 --> 00:34:33,862
Since when did you, Brass, start
giving a damn about other people?

601
00:34:34,080 --> 00:34:36,845
Well, now that you know
about the grand plan...

602
00:34:37,640 --> 00:34:38,720
You're stuck here.

603
00:34:38,900 --> 00:34:41,060
We can't risk letting you go. Sorry.

604
00:34:42,040 --> 00:34:45,687
Actually, there's something I've
been meaning to ask you boys.

605
00:34:46,480 --> 00:34:47,880
So, tell me.

606
00:34:48,320 --> 00:34:52,320
Is it true that you brats are hiding
treasure somewhere around here?

607
00:35:20,560 --> 00:35:22,517
Stupid dog huh?

608
00:35:22,600 --> 00:35:23,637
Hey! Wait!

609
00:35:23,720 --> 00:35:24,897
What's that?

610
00:35:24,980 --> 00:35:31,037
Something weird is

611
00:35:31,120 --> 00:35:32,708
happening in Gray Terminal.

612
00:35:33,000 --> 00:35:34,235
That looks like fire.

613
00:35:38,740 --> 00:35:41,580
Who knew the plan would
turn out to be this fun?

614
00:35:42,240 --> 00:35:44,100
Hey, boss, come quick.

615
00:35:44,240 --> 00:35:45,420
You gotta see this.

616
00:35:46,000 --> 00:35:48,080
All right, what's the big deal? Mr.

617
00:35:48,200 --> 00:35:49,120
Skye, look.

618
00:35:49,720 --> 00:35:50,860
Is that the town?

619
00:35:51,100 --> 00:35:52,629
No, it's closer than that.

620
00:35:52,860 --> 00:35:54,137
I think it's Grey Terminal.

621
00:35:54,220 --> 00:35:55,140
It's on fire.

622
00:35:57,320 --> 00:35:58,400
What's going on?

623
00:35:58,520 --> 00:35:59,977
Where's that smoke coming from?

624
00:36:00,060 --> 00:36:02,317
Grey Terminal has never
caught fire before.

625
00:36:02,400 --> 00:36:03,280
What happened?

626
00:36:04,940 --> 00:36:06,517
Edge Town is too dangerous.

627
00:36:06,600 --> 00:36:07,835
Evacuate immediately.

628
00:36:07,920 --> 00:36:10,038
All residents, please head downtown.

629
00:36:10,840 --> 00:36:12,500
Stay here where it's safe.

630
00:36:12,680 --> 00:36:15,386
We'll take care of the
fire and other citizen.

631
00:36:19,060 --> 00:36:20,160
Everybody, get up!

632
00:36:20,300 --> 00:36:21,241
We gotta escape!

633
00:36:24,300 --> 00:36:26,480
The fire almost has us surrounded.

634
00:36:26,760 --> 00:36:28,617
Where did this mess even come from?

635
00:36:28,700 --> 00:36:30,053
Look, it's no use, man.

636
00:36:30,160 --> 00:36:32,395
Leave it behind and make a run for it.

637
00:36:35,000 --> 00:36:35,830
Crap!

638
00:36:35,913 --> 00:36:37,857
The fire's already gotten to the shore!

639
00:36:37,940 --> 00:36:40,411
The entrance to the forest is burning too!

640
00:36:40,560 --> 00:36:42,900
We're all gonna die! Where do we go?

641
00:36:47,140 --> 00:36:49,520
Say so long to this dump, fellas.

642
00:36:49,940 --> 00:36:50,900
Good riddance!

643
00:36:52,180 --> 00:36:54,680
It'll be easy living from here on out.

644
00:36:55,200 --> 00:36:57,340
Yeah, just like the nobles.

645
00:36:59,400 --> 00:37:00,520
Of course not.

646
00:37:00,820 --> 00:37:04,917
We couldn't care less about the living
garbage stinking up Gray Terminal.

647
00:37:05,000 --> 00:37:07,040
But it makes a good hideout.

648
00:37:07,340 --> 00:37:10,940
The place is huge, plus no
law around to bug us, get it?

649
00:37:11,180 --> 00:37:12,420
I'm aware of that.

650
00:37:12,540 --> 00:37:17,800
But think, if you do this for me,
well, you won't need a hideout.

651
00:37:18,240 --> 00:37:23,100
I have the authority to make you
and your crew Bone Fight nobles.

652
00:37:24,600 --> 00:37:25,430
Really?

653
00:37:25,513 --> 00:37:26,620
You do that for us?

654
00:37:27,440 --> 00:37:30,920
Once this is through, the King
of Goa will give us titles.

655
00:37:31,240 --> 00:37:33,400
We'll live in high-townest nobles.

656
00:37:33,600 --> 00:37:35,188
No more of this trash heap.

657
00:37:42,060 --> 00:37:43,460
Now, let's move.

658
00:37:43,740 --> 00:37:44,799
We're almost done.

659
00:37:44,980 --> 00:37:45,940
And don't worry.

660
00:37:46,580 --> 00:37:47,840
On to the Great Gate.

661
00:37:48,040 --> 00:37:49,797
The military is waiting for us.

662
00:37:49,880 --> 00:37:52,437
Captain, we left those
two brats in the hideout.

663
00:37:52,520 --> 00:37:53,350
Forget them.

664
00:37:53,460 --> 00:37:56,497
They had their chance to join up when
I asked them where their treasure was.

665
00:37:56,580 --> 00:38:01,600
But they blew it fools like
them are gonna live long anyway

666
00:38:05,680 --> 00:38:08,780
Captain the gate is already
closed. It's nothing.

667
00:38:09,020 --> 00:38:11,137
They just don't want other
people to break in and cause

668
00:38:11,220 --> 00:38:14,217
a riot I'm supposed to give
them a sign once we're here.

669
00:38:14,300 --> 00:38:15,653
Then they'll open it up

670
00:38:16,800 --> 00:38:18,080
It's me blue jam.

671
00:38:18,340 --> 00:38:19,170
We're here

672
00:38:22,700 --> 00:38:25,060
Huh hey open the damn gate

673
00:38:30,260 --> 00:38:33,580
Captain, you don't think...

674
00:38:34,380 --> 00:38:35,960
Hey! Come on!

675
00:38:36,080 --> 00:38:37,377
What the hell are you doing?!

676
00:38:37,460 --> 00:38:38,460
This isn't funny!

677
00:38:38,560 --> 00:38:39,390
Open the gate!

678
00:38:39,660 --> 00:38:40,940
We made a deal!

679
00:38:41,120 --> 00:38:43,557
You're supposed to let us
evacuate from this pit!

680
00:38:43,640 --> 00:38:47,100
Quit screwing around and let
us in, you bunch of bastards!

681
00:38:47,680 --> 00:38:49,360
The King made me a promise!

682
00:38:49,600 --> 00:38:51,957
If we burn down a terminal,
he'd make us nobles!

683
00:38:52,040 --> 00:38:52,900
Don't tell me!

684
00:38:54,620 --> 00:38:57,400
The king set us up! That liar!

685
00:38:58,200 --> 00:38:59,120
Damn it!

686
00:39:01,020 --> 00:39:01,880
Did you hear?

687
00:39:02,060 --> 00:39:03,857
They found out who started the fire.

688
00:39:03,940 --> 00:39:06,957
It was some pirate named
Blue Jam from Grey Terminal.

689
00:39:07,040 --> 00:39:08,200
How despicable.

690
00:39:08,580 --> 00:39:10,680
A criminal turning on his own men.

691
00:39:10,900 --> 00:39:12,997
I bet he was trying to
keep the world government's

692
00:39:13,080 --> 00:39:15,717
observers away so he could
keep on terrorizing people.

693
00:39:15,800 --> 00:39:17,329
Gosh, what an evil pirate.

694
00:39:21,620 --> 00:39:23,060
It's way too hot, Ace!

695
00:39:23,180 --> 00:39:24,533
I think I'm gonna melt!

696
00:39:24,740 --> 00:39:26,480
Oh, you are! Damn!

697
00:39:26,700 --> 00:39:28,817
Why did Blue Jam rope us into this mess?

698
00:39:28,900 --> 00:39:30,120
We can't get away!

699
00:39:30,280 --> 00:39:31,456
I don't want to die!

700
00:39:32,120 --> 00:39:34,767
If you don't stop
complaining, I'll kill you!

701
00:39:35,060 --> 00:39:36,140
It's not that hot!

702
00:39:38,320 --> 00:39:39,150
I'm burning!

703
00:39:39,360 --> 00:39:40,517
I mean, this isn't so bad!

704
00:39:40,600 --> 00:39:41,957
It's all over the place!

705
00:39:42,040 --> 00:39:43,460
I can barely breathe!

706
00:39:44,060 --> 00:39:45,157
I mean, I'm cool!

707
00:39:45,240 --> 00:39:47,440
The fire will kill us all!

708
00:39:47,640 --> 00:39:49,840
We're gonna be fine! Don't worry.

709
00:39:50,840 --> 00:39:52,660
We'll live. Somehow.

710
00:39:53,460 --> 00:39:54,620
Hey, are you nuts?

711
00:39:54,760 --> 00:39:56,277
You're going the wrong way!

712
00:39:56,360 --> 00:39:57,780
Open the gate now!

713
00:39:58,140 --> 00:39:59,728
What are you talking about?

714
00:40:00,880 --> 00:40:01,720
Don't, brat!

715
00:40:02,300 --> 00:40:03,260
Go home!

716
00:40:05,180 --> 00:40:07,540
Luffy! Ace! Run!

717
00:40:12,480 --> 00:40:13,697
Let go, brat!

718
00:40:13,780 --> 00:40:15,440
Stay away from the lock.

719
00:40:15,700 --> 00:40:17,340
Open the gate.

720
00:40:19,200 --> 00:40:20,030
Stop.

721
00:40:20,640 --> 00:40:21,470
No.

722
00:40:29,460 --> 00:40:31,897
Why don't you be a good
kid and get out of here?

723
00:40:31,980 --> 00:40:33,804
Don't give us any more trouble.

724
00:40:37,020 --> 00:40:39,680
I'm sorry, guys.

725
00:41:02,360 --> 00:41:04,020
What happened to you, boy?

726
00:41:10,580 --> 00:41:11,460
Who's there?

727
00:41:15,900 --> 00:41:20,500
Whoever you are, listen, the nobles
are the ones behind this fire.

728
00:41:23,200 --> 00:41:24,860
You gotta believe me.

729
00:41:26,840 --> 00:41:29,840
Hightown wreaks worse than
Great Terminal ever did.

730
00:41:29,940 --> 00:41:33,780
The people act civilized, but on
the inside, they're all rotten.

731
00:41:34,100 --> 00:41:38,337
They only care about making themselves
look good no matter what it takes.

732
00:41:38,420 --> 00:41:40,100
I can't stay here.

733
00:41:40,240 --> 00:41:42,181
If I do, then I'll never be free.

734
00:41:46,340 --> 00:41:48,420
I'm ashamed of being born noble.

735
00:41:48,700 --> 00:41:49,820
I hate myself.

736
00:41:50,520 --> 00:41:51,540
Go, Kingdom.

737
00:41:51,880 --> 00:41:53,797
Look what you've done to this child.

738
00:41:53,880 --> 00:41:55,880
How you've turned him against you.

739
00:41:57,080 --> 00:41:58,720
I know how you feel.

740
00:41:59,500 --> 00:42:01,760
I was born in this country, too.

741
00:42:03,200 --> 00:42:06,435
But I alone do not have the
power to change this world.

742
00:42:06,620 --> 00:42:08,080
And maybe I never will.

743
00:42:08,680 --> 00:42:09,797
But at least...

744
00:42:09,880 --> 00:42:12,357
At least you're actually
listening to me, aren't you?

745
00:42:12,440 --> 00:42:15,440
Of course I am, and I'll never forget.
